# CVE-2026-115905 — zip parser differential / "Zip Cloaking" (arbitrary file
# overwrite on EXTRACTION of crafted archives), fixed in zip 9.0.5.
#
# Accepted risk (CTO, 29 Oct 2026):
# - zip 3.0.0 enters ONLY as a build-dependency of utoipa-swagger-ui v9 (its
#   build.rs extracts the vendored swagger-ui-dist assets at compile time).
# - Rungu never extracts untrusted archives at runtime; the inputs are the
#   crate's own published vendored assets, not attacker-controlled.
# - zip >= 9.0.5 requires utoipa-swagger-ui v10, which requires utoipa ^6
#   (Rungu pins utoipa 5 across ~20 route files) — tracked as a dedicated
#   migration issue, not a drive-by bump.
# - Advisory is currently Trivy-only (no RustSec entry; cargo audit clean).
# Remove this entry when utoipa-swagger-ui v10 migration lands.
CVE-2026-115905
